    "turn_text": "It's sometimes like, like I know here in North Dakota, and I don't want to pick on North Dakota, because again, I think most of our cops in North Dakota, good cops, good people, I don't want to pick on anybody. But in North Dakota, I mean, sometimes I'll watch the review process. And even when I agree with the outcome and say, okay, well, they probably reach the right conclusion, a lot of times when we're investigating, you know, was this use of force appropriate or whatnot, it's another law enforcement agency doing the investigation, which almost kind of seems like I mean, the thin blue wine that everybody talks about cuts across departments and levels of law enforcement. Is it fair to have other law enforcement officials investigate law enforcement officials? Aren't they just going to view these things all through the same lens?",
