  {
    "episode_id": 47158,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47158.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "I think anybody who's followed the legislature and saw how many bills you worked on coming out of the Senate Judiciary Committee is aware of that. And aware of frankly, and I've always appreciated your very nuanced approach to this because I have the same approach. I mean, a lot of times conservatives and Republicans, the expectation is that we just sort of back the cops and the Democrats don't. I mean, that's, that's a very unfair and very generalized position. I appreciate a nuanced approach to this. I think that, you know, it's, it's capable of saying the cops are great people and they're doing a tough job and we appreciate them, but also there are problems and it needs reform. You can do that. and what I worry about when people like Zach, what he's doing here, and I understand what he's doing, and the argument he's trying to make, but it's",
