        "text": "Militarizing police culture undermines trust between law enforcement and civilian communities.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Police should not perceive their role as inherently adversarial toward civilians.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      },
      {
        "text": "The use of war metaphors in policing distorts legitimate public safety functions.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "Civilians have inherent rights to safety and dignity that are compromised when treated as enemies.",
        "confidence": 0.84
      },
      {
        "text": "A shift in cultural mindset is necessary before structural reforms in policing can succeed.",
