    "turn_idx": 91,
    "turn_text": "I often tell people that one of the moments in history that makes me proudest to be an American was when the ACLU of all organizations defended the right of the Ku Klux Klan to hold a march in Skokie, Illinois. I was proud of it. Not because I like the Ku Klux Klan or because I want those racist idiots to be marching down the streets. I'd really prefer they just shut up, but they're Americans too. They have First Amendment rights too. And an organization whose principles are generally completely antithetical to those of the Klan stepped in and supported their First Amendment rights. To me,",
