    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47158.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 94,
    "turn_text": "Well, exactly. The Klan is a horrible, horrible people. But still, it's that sort of commitment to principle that I think is the real test of our society. Like, we don't need the First Amendment to protect discussions about the weather. We need the First Amendment to protect discussions that make a lot of people angry. you know, whether it's the Klan or, and again, I'm not comparing, the Klan is not comparable to any of the protests that are happening now at all. That's not the comparison I'm making. I'm saying... A lot of times when things get volatile, protests are good. Even when I absolutely disagree with everything the protesters are saying, I want them to be able to protest. I don't want anybody to be able to burn some innocent business owners down. If you're setting fires and throwing rocks and doing that stuff, this is no longer a peaceful assembly. So that's the point. Okay.",
